"kme":0.249811,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.32433,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000141376","module":"yellow","kme":0.24534,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.41964,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000141376","module":"grey60","kme":0.267265,"hub":true,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.817457,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000141376","module":"blue","kme":0.191462,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.415372,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000141376","entrez_id":["54828"],"uniprot":["Q9H6U6"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables several functions, including acetyltransferase activator activity; beta-tubulin binding activity; and histone acetyltransferase binding activity. Involved in cellular response to estrogen stimulus; positive regulation of catalytic activity; and positive regulation of transcription by RNA polymerase II. Located in nucleus; phagophore assembly site; and transcriptionally active chromatin. Biomarker of breast cancer. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9H6U6","text":"Plays a role in angiogenesis. Participates in the regulation of cell polarity and directional endothelial cell migration by mediating both the activation and recruitment of CDC42 and the reorganization of the actin cytoskeleton at the cell leading edge. Promotes filipodia formation (By similarity). Functions synergistically with PELP1 as a transcriptional coactivator of estrogen receptor-responsive genes. Stimulates histone acetyltransferase activity. Binds to chromatin. Plays a regulatory role in autophagic activity. In complex with PHAF1, associates with the preautophagosomal structure during both non-selective and selective autophagy (PubMed:33499712). Probably binds phosphatidylinositol 3-phosphate (PtdIns3P) which would mediate the recruitment preautophagosomal structures (PubMed:33499712)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}